From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: s5k5e9: propagate I2C errors and start at 1x analogue gain

Optional robustness fix for the q706f second rear camera (S5K5E9). It is NOT
needed for VBLANK support: the driver already exposes a writable
V4L2_CID_VBLANK (frame_length_lines 0x0340), a read-only V4L2_CID_HBLANK,
V4L2_CID_PIXEL_RATE, and updates the V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE range to
height + vblank - 2 whenever VBLANK changes, which is everything libcamera's
CameraSensor and the AGC frame-duration series need.

What it fixes:
  - s5k5e9_set_ctrl() wrote group-hold on / register / group-hold off and
    kept only the last return value, so a failed exposure, gain or VBLANK
    write (we have seen CCI timeouts on this bus at boot) was reported as
    success. The three writes now go through s5k5e9_write_held(), which
    always releases the hold and returns the first error.
  - s5k5e9_write_reg_list() returned only the status of the last register;
    it now stops at the first failing write (stream start then fails
    loudly instead of streaming with a half-programmed sensor).
  - V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN defaulted to 1024 (32x, the maximum), applied by
    __v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup() at every stream start until userspace sets a
    gain. Default to 32 (1x).

Risk: if some register in the init tables is NACKed today without visible
effect, stream start now fails with "Cannot write register"; revert this
patch in that case. Not tested on the device.

Status: .pending (not applied by the build). Applies with patch -p1 -F0 on
top of 0001..0120.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e9.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e9.c
@@ -194,12 +194,35 @@
 
 static int s5k5e9_write_reg_list(struct s5k5e9 *s5k5e9, const struct s5k5e9_reg_list *reg_list)
 {
-	int ret = 0;
+	int ret;
 
-	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < reg_list->num_of_regs; i++)
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, reg_list->regs[i].address, 1, reg_list->regs[i].val);
+	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < reg_list->num_of_regs; i++) {
+		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, reg_list->regs[i].address, 1,
+				   reg_list->regs[i].val);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Write one SMIA register inside a grouped parameter hold (0x0104) so that
+ * the sensor latches it at a frame boundary. The hold is always released,
+ * and the first error is returned instead of being overwritten.
+ */
+static int s5k5e9_write_held(struct s5k5e9 *s5k5e9, u16 reg, u16 len, u32 val)
+{
+	int ret, ret2;
+
+	ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x01);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, reg, len, val);
+	ret2 = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x00);
+
+	return ret ? ret : ret2;
 }
 
 static int s5k5e9_read(struct s5k5e9 *s5k5e9, u16 reg, u16 len, u32 *val)
@@ -452,19 +475,14 @@
 
 	switch (ctrl->id) {
 	case V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE:
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x01);
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0202, 2, ctrl->val);
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x00);
+		ret = s5k5e9_write_held(s5k5e9, 0x0202, 2, ctrl->val);
 		break;
 	case V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN:
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x01);
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0204, 2, ctrl->val);
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x00);
+		ret = s5k5e9_write_held(s5k5e9, 0x0204, 2, ctrl->val);
 		break;
 	case V4L2_CID_VBLANK:
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x01);
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0340, 2, s5k5e9->cur_mode->height + ctrl->val);
-		ret = s5k5e9_write(s5k5e9, 0x0104, 1, 0x00);
+		ret = s5k5e9_write_held(s5k5e9, 0x0340, 2,
+					s5k5e9->cur_mode->height + ctrl->val);
 		break;
 	default:
 		ret = -EINVAL;
@@ -606,8 +624,9 @@
 						 exposure_max, 1,
 						 exposure_max);
 
+	/* Code 32 = 1x (SMIA analogue_gain_code_global); start at 1x, not 32x. */
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(handler, &s5k5e9_ctrl_ops, V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN,
-			  32, 1024, 1, 1024);
+			  32, 1024, 1, 32);
 
 	if (handler->error) {
 		ret = handler->error;
